    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. There's exactly one concrete test class (`AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is an abstract helper), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" behavior for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with getters/setters, mapped to new columns. These must persist because the test reads them back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` after creation.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them (MapStruct auto-maps them by name).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the existing hard-duplicate (409) check passes, it computes `possibleDuplicateOf(owner)`: an existing owner with the same normalized last name and the same (non-blank) postcode but a different telephone. If found, `possibleDuplicate` is set true with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to that owner's id (lowest id when several qualify, for determinism); otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is false and no reference is recorded. A candidate with no postcode never soft-matches.\n\nThe soft-match runs only after the hard-duplicate check, so genuine duplicates are still rejected with 409 while soft matches are created and flagged.",
